      <p>Perform the tape-adhesion and color-contrast evaluation:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>The Cross-Hatch Tape Adhesion Test:</strong> Use a cutter to make a small X in the existing paint in an inconspicuous corner. Press a piece of strong duct tape over the X and rip it off sharply. If paint flakes off with the tape, the existing paint is failing; it must be scraped, puttied, and <strong>primed</strong>. If the paint remains intact, the base is sound.</li>
        <li><strong>You can SAFELY SKIP a full primer coat if:</strong>
