        <li><strong>Missing, breached, or degraded Damp-Proof Course (DPC):</strong> The Damp-Proof Course is a 40mm to 50mm thick waterproof concrete or bituminous membrane cast horizontally atop the foundation plinth beam during construction. In older Indian buildings, or in rushed builder constructions, the DPC is either completely missing, compromised by plumbing pipe penetrations, or bridged by external garden soil levels built up above the plinth.</li>
