      <p>You've tightened the tap as far as it'll go, and it's still dripping into the basin. Or worse — it's a modern single-lever basin mixer that just won't stop weeping from the spout no matter what position you set it to. Basin and sink faucets today aren't all the same simple washer-and-spindle design your grandfather's plumber dealt with — many modern fixtures have ceramic disc cartridges inside. Diagnosing the actual internal cause before you start disassembling anything is the key to a fast, permanent fix. Here is how to figure out what is broken and fix it yourself in under 30 minutes.</p>

