      <h3>Part B: Applying Electrical Insulation Tape Properly</h3>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Ensure a tight mechanical joint:</strong> Strip 2 cm of clean copper from both conductors and twist them together with pliers in a tight Western Union or pigtail splice. Tape is meant to insulate a solid physical joint, not hold loose wires together.</li>
